  "id": "horizontalvertical-illusion",
  "term": "horizontal–vertical illusion",
  "definition": "The horizontal–vertical illusion is a visual effect involving horizontal and vertical lines in which their perceived lengths are misestimated. In the source, it is used as a stimulus to compare how people judge line length in direct perception and in mental imagery.",
